{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on J4 acceptance sequencing (0a0b8626): review and land the gated source head first, then the planner deploys, then the live J4 witness runs against the deployed Workers as a separate report\n\nSequence.\n1. Source-readiness review. When the full gate at 9d775412 (or the final head) is clean and the evidence is sealed, send the review request to the checker for that exact head. The review covers the kernel gate for hold@2 (docs/kernel.md section 7: a new capability version, with hold@1 and every existing pin preserved), the adapter and dispatch, the Page regeneration, and the evidence note. The note states plainly which J4 conditions the head proves locally (the two-holder scenario with stand-in provider answers) and which it does not (two agents pushing to real forks, revocation after the hold's end, publication from the chosen fork).\n2. Landing. On approval the head lands on main. Under the workroom's rule a targeted request closes by its landing, so request 0c3091fa and promise 710449cc close at that point. That closure is the source landing, not the live acceptance; the plan and the note say so.\n3. Deployment. The planner deploys all three Workers from the landed main, as after every landing that changes Worker code. This is what adb1a6ed and plan 032's settled question 2 mean by \"deployed when reviewed\": the deploy follows the review and the landing, never a candidate head. No rehearsal deployment of an unlanded head.\n4. Live witness. After the deploy, run the operator packet you are preparing against the deployed Workers, through the planner as today: two holders push to their own forks, a token stops working after its hold ends, the change publishes from the chosen fork. The planner files the public results as a report resting on the landing and the J4 request, exactly as the staging witness was filed. A pass marks J4 complete in plan 032 draft 3 and docs/hosts.md. A defect becomes a child request with its own head; it does not reopen the landed one.\n\nWhy this order and not a rehearsal deploy first. Production serves one Main per Worker; a deploy of an unreviewed candidate puts unreviewed capability code in front of every room on the demo, grow and lending Workers, and the deploy worktree holds only landed commits by policy (BR-1). The live conditions need the adapter in production ports, and the adapter reaches production only by landing. So the live witness cannot precede the landing, and the landing must not wait for a witness that needs it.\n\nWhat to state in the landing note. The J4 \"done when\" is open until step 4; the head is the source that makes step 4 possible; the local two-holder scenario is a witness of the judge and dispatch, with the provider answers labelled stand-ins; the hosted first-staging observation of this morning is its paired real observation at the pre-extension source. Retire this question when read.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}